Why the application lives on V1
-------------------------------
cadmus-vulnshop-cpp-cr is POSIX C++ (sockets, unistd.h, popen) and its dynamic
analysis tier - Valgrind, AddressSanitizer, UBSan - only exists on Linux. You
work from SC1, but the code is built and run on V1:

  1. Open VS Code, press F1, choose "Remote-SSH: Connect to Host..." and pick v1.
     Password: {{ cr12_trainee_password }}. (The first connection takes a minute - VS Code
     installs its server on V1.)
  2. File -> Open Folder -> {{ cr12_app_dir }}
  3. Terminal -> New Terminal opens a shell ON V1. Everything in the lab guide
     that starts with ./ or ~/lab-tools/ is typed there.

Without VS Code:  open "V1 terminal" on the desktop, or type  ssh v1  in a
Windows terminal.

